xsys/ — recipe for the darwin/ppc32 (Mac OS X 10.5 Leopard) tables of the
vendored golang.org/x/sys/unix (goppc-jic6x.3)
==============================================================================

Purpose
-------
`cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix` and `cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/term` had no
darwin/ppc32 build files, so `go/types` TestStdlib could not typecheck them on
a ppc32 GOROOT and the 179 identifiers of x/sys/unix (plus 23 cascading x/term
names) were undefined.  This directory holds everything needed to regenerate
the nine port-local files that fix that, byte for byte:

  cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix/ztypes_darwin_ppc.go      (target: cgo)
  cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix/zerrors_darwin_ppc.go     (target: mkerrors)
  cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix/zsyscall_darwin_ppc.go    (host: mksyscall)
  cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix/zsyscall_darwin_ppc.s     (host: mkasm)
  cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix/zsysnum_darwin_ppc.go     (host: mksysnum)
and the inputs for the four hand-written files (not generated here; committed
verbatim, see contract §5 H3):

  syscall_darwin_ppc.go, absent_darwin_ppc.go, asm_darwin_ppc.s,
  syscall_darwin_libcdir.go (the verbatim move of commit C1)

`testdata` is invisible to the go tool, to TestStdlib and to `go mod vendor`, so
this recipe survives the operations that delete the generated files.

Upstream base
-------------
golang.org/x/sys v0.39.0, origin go.googlesource.com/sys@08e54827f670,
module hash h1:CvCKL8MeisomCi6qNZ+wbb0DN9E5AATixKsvNtMoMFk= (== src/cmd/go.sum:17);
golang.org/x/term v0.38.0, h1:PQ5pkm/rLO6HnxFR7N2lJHOZX6Kez5Y1gDSJla6jo7Q=
(== src/cmd/go.sum:21).  The seven upstream generator sources are pinned in
`xsys-generators.sha256`; gen-host.sh refuses to run if the module copy differs.
The whole vendored tree is upstream v0.39.0 except the files listed under
"Vendored divergences" below.  x/term is unmodified.

Decisions
---------
1. **Option A (supervisor, 2026-10-22).**  Upstream's darwin `Getdirentries`
   is implemented through fdopendir/readdir_r.  Leopard's libSystem has no
   `fdopendir`, and Go binds darwin dynamic imports non-lazily at launch, so
   that wrapper cannot even be reached on ppc32.  Commit C1 moves the function
   and `fdopendir` verbatim into `syscall_darwin_libcdir.go`, tagged
   `//go:build darwin && !ppc`; darwin/ppc32 provides `Getdirentries` in
   `syscall_darwin_ppc.go` with the raw `SYS_GETDIRENTRIES64` system call
   (344; xnu-1228 syscalls.master, off_t * stored as a full 8 bytes by the
   kernel).  amd64/arm64 behaviour is unchanged (A5 API identity).

2. **Absent-function policy.**  The 23 `//sys` declarations in
   `leopard-absent-sys.txt` name libc symbols that `nm -g -arch ppc
   /usr/lib/libSystem.B.dylib` on the iBook (libSystem 111.1.7) does not
   define.  gen-host.sh removes those declarations before mksyscall runs, and
   `syscall_darwin_ppc.go` supplies the Go functions: 12 return ENOSYS, and
   the 11 `*at` functions emulate AT_FDCWD with the path-based calls and
   return ENOTSUP for any other dirfd.  Failing explicitly beats silently
   operating on the wrong file, and `unix.UtimesNano` already falls back to
   `utimes` on ENOSYS.  This mirrors std darwin/ppc (`src/syscall`).

3. **ABSENT compatibility identifiers.**  14 identifiers that generic vendored
   code references do not exist in Leopard's headers (`AT_FDCWD`, the other
   `AT_*`, `AF_VSOCK`, `RawSockaddrVM`, `SaEndpoints`, `SaeAssocID`,
   `SaeConnID`, `IPMreqn`, `IPv6MTUInfo`, `TCPConnectionInfo` and their
   `Sizeof*`).  They live in `absent_darwin_ppc.go`, marked ABSENT, with the
   ppc32 Go layout; every use fails in the Leopard kernel or in the ENOSYS /
   ENOTSUP wrappers.  Nothing else is invented: names Leopard lacks that
   upstream references elsewhere (Syscall9, Inet4Pktinfo, XVSockPCB, XSocket64,
   XVSockPgen, VMADDR_*, CLOCK_*, UTIME_*, Timeval32, XSocket, XSockbuf) stay
   undefined, and code that names them fails to compile.

4. **Legacy (unsuffixed) libc symbols, shared with std.**  As in std
   darwin/ppc32, the imports are the legacy entry points, not their
   `$UNIX2003` twins, and struct layouts are pinned to `__DARWIN_UNIX03 0`
   (the `#define` at the top of `types_darwin_leopard.go`).  This is
   internally consistent and matches std's hardware-validated choice; a
   port-wide decision on legacy vs POSIX/`$UNIX2003` semantics is still open
   (contract §8 residual risk 1).

5. **No Syscall9.**  darwin/ppc32 std has no `syscall.Syscall9`, so x/sys
   cannot offer `unix.Syscall9`.  API parity exception, documented in
   `asm_darwin_ppc.s`.

6. **Generator inputs may only lose declarations proven ABSENT.**  The target
   inputs (`types_darwin_leopard.go`, `mkerrors.sh`, `xsys_sizes.c`) are
   copies of the upstream files with the changes recorded in
   `types_darwin_leopard.patch` and `mkerrors-leopard.patch`; each deletion is
   backed by a read-only grep of the Leopard SDK recorded in
   runs/jic6x-3-gen-ibook-20261022T152445Z/input-changes-{1,2,3}.md.

