`types_darwin_leopard.go` == `golang.org/x/sys@v0.39.0/unix/types_darwin.go`
+ `types_darwin_leopard.patch`; `mkerrors.sh` == the module's `mkerrors.sh` +
`mkerrors-leopard.patch` (both checked with `patch`, 2026-10-22).  The patches
were generated against the hash-verified module copy, so the `---` path they
name is the module's, not a worktree path; apply them with an explicit file
argument (`patch out.go < types_darwin_leopard.patch`) or `-p1` on a copy whose
name matches the `+++` line.

Target generation outputs (produced on the iBook by the run below; not stored
here because they are transcribed into the two committed tables):

  622a93687e179aeed6ffed8bbb726b9d19754e52a97c22d5d2a7654b0f8249a4  ztypes.raw
  29ee7a550687f050c0258ff45043f6a87b840a32280e19ee6cef3f6e266c39cb  zerrors.raw
  955f2eff828f8b62de7407ab24e1436446088a4559b28239e946bb568ae81cb2  xsys_sizes.txt

`xsys_sizes.txt` (committed here) is the C `sizeof` transcription check for 62
types, measured by the same iBook gcc in the generation session.  It is
comparison evidence, not a grade: the grading oracle for the 42 overlapping
types and 109 measured rows is the pmg5 C-probe data in
`src/syscall/testdata/darwin_ppc32/layout.txt`, and the constant oracle is
`constants.txt`.

Generators and their inputs (what makes each output)
----------------------------------------------------
* `ztypes_darwin_ppc.go`     `go tool cgo -godefs types_darwin_leopard.go` on
                             the target, then `go run mkpost.go` on the host.
                             Target changes vs upstream `types_darwin.go`:
                             drop `<sys/vsock.h>`, `#include <sys/types.h>`
                             before `<sys/kern_control.h>`, `stat_t`/`statfs_t`
                             select `struct stat64`/`struct statfs64` for
                             `__ppc__` as well, delete the ABSENT
                             vsock/xsocket/sae/ip_mreqn/ip6_mtuinfo/tcp_conn
                             declarations and the `AT_*` block, spell the C
                             types cgo cannot classify (`_C_*`, `_Gid_t`,
                             `_Socklen`, `FdSet`) directly, and drop
                             `Timeval32`/`XSocket`/`XSockbuf` (Leopard never
                             completes those types).
* `zerrors_darwin_ppc.go`    `bash mkerrors.sh` on the target; the Leopard
                             copy removes `#include <sys/clonefile.h>`,
                             `<sys/vsock.h>`, `<sys/stdio.h>` and adds
                             `<netinet/ip_mroute.h>` (SIOCGETSGCNT /
                             SIOCGETVIFCNT, as std's mkerrors.sh does).
* `zsyscall_darwin_ppc.go`   `mksyscall.go -b32 -tags darwin,ppc` on
                             `syscall_bsd.go` + a *filtered* copy of
                             `syscall_darwin.go` + `syscall_darwin_ppc.go`.
* `zsyscall_darwin_ppc.s`    `mkasm.go darwin ppc` with the one-line
                             `mkasm-ppc.patch` (`archPtrSize` learns
                             `"ppc": 4`); the generated `darwin_ppc_test.go`
                             is deleted.
* `zsysnum_darwin_ppc.go`    `perl src/syscall/mksysnum_darwin.pl` on
                             `reference/xnu/bsd/sys/syscall.h`
                             (md5 33dfdddbb1866a4e524711b01d59aebe, identical
                             to the iBook SDK's), `package syscall` →
                             `package unix`, and the one rename below.

Syscall-202 rename: std's `mksysnum_darwin.pl` emits `SYS___SYSCTL = 202`.
x/sys spells entry 202 `SYS_SYSCTL` in `zsysnum_darwin_{amd64,arm64}.go` and
provides `const SYS___SYSCTL = SYS_SYSCTL` in `syscall_darwin.go:101`, so the
generated file is renamed to `SYS_SYSCTL` and must not declare
`SYS___SYSCTL`.  gen-host.sh asserts that exactly one line was renamed; the
line count (338) and every value are unchanged.

Regeneration
------------
Host part (pure Go/perl; needs the worktree's `bin/go` and a hash-verified
x/sys v0.39.0 module copy):

    mkdir -p $SCR/stage && gen-host.sh $XSYS $WT $SCR/stage [ztypes.raw zerrors.raw]

`XSYS` is `<GOMODCACHE>/golang.org/x/sys@v0.39.0`, `WT` the Go worktree,
`$SCR/stage` an empty directory.  Outputs: `zsyscall_darwin_ppc.{go,s}`,
`zsysnum_darwin_ppc.go`, plus `ztypes_darwin_ppc.go` and `zerrors_darwin_ppc.go`
when the target raws are given.  Nothing is copied into the worktree; copy the
files explicitly and re-insert the provenance header (the committed tables have
a `// Port-local generation provenance` block after the `Code generated` line —
see `git show C2 -- ztypes_darwin_ppc.go`).

Target part (native darwin/ppc Go on Leopard, run on the iBook; never on the
shared GOROOT — upload this directory to /tmp and run there):

    tar -C <this dir> -cf - . | ssh ibook 'mkdir /tmp/jic6x3-gen-TS && tar -C /tmp/jic6x3-gen-TS -xpf -'
    ssh ibook '...bounded-run.sh --cpu 0 --wall 1800 --prefix jic6x3-gen-full \
        -- /bin/bash /tmp/jic6x3-gen-TS/gen-target.sh /tmp/jic6x3-gen-TS'
    scp ibook:/tmp/jic6x3-gen-TS/{ztypes.raw,zerrors.raw,xsys_sizes.txt,rc.txt,host-identity.txt} .

`gen-target.sh` sets `GOOS=darwin GOARCH=ppc CGO_ENABLED=1 GOENV=off
GO111MODULE=off GOTOOLCHAIN=local CC=$PWD/cc-ppc.sh` and runs `mkerrors.sh`,
`go tool cgo -godefs types_darwin_leopard.go` and `xsys_sizes.c`.  Every Go
workload on the target goes through `tools/harness/bounded-run.sh`; the three
rc values in `rc.txt` must be 0.  `cc-ppc.sh` execs `/usr/bin/gcc -arch ppc`
after stripping `-fno-lto` (Tigerbrew gcc wrappers add it).  A
`cc-ppc64.sh`/`godefs-preflight.go` pair is used only for the G0 negative
control and is deliberately not committed.

