  baselines, the libSystem ppc symbol list, the Leopard SDK presence tables,
  the amd64 libc import list, the before/after `go list` and `go doc -all`
  baselines, and pf1–pf7.  Read-only for every lane.
* `runs/jic6x-3-impl-20261022T150719Z/` — L1: C1, the host generation
  (`h4-gen-host-stage1.log`), A6(a) with its two negative controls (`a6/`),
  the 13-file kit (`h5-kit.sha256`).
* `runs/jic6x-3-gen-ibook-20261022T152445Z/` — L2: the three target
  invocations, the generated raws, `host-identity.txt`, and the input-change
  records `input-changes-{1,2,3}.md` + `kit-inv3/`.
* `runs/jic6x-3-impl-20261022T154034Z/` — L3: the integration run
  (`h6-gen-host-stage2.log` regenerates all five tables), the A1–A8/A12/A13
  gate logs, the probe source, and the A7 counts.
* `runs/jic6x-3-hw-<TS>/` — L4: the iBook hardware legs (TestStdlib, the
  probe, the mutant), the overlay manifest and the cleanup record.
* Contract: `docs/jic6x-3-darwin-ppc-tables.md`; bead `goppc-jic6x.3`.

Vendored divergences
--------------------
`cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix` differs from v0.39.0 in exactly these files
(A2):

  syscall_darwin.go        C1: fdopendir + darwin Getdirentries moved out
  syscall_darwin_libcdir.go  C1: new, `darwin && !ppc`, the moved code verbatim
  syscall_darwin_ppc.go    new, port-local (arch helpers, Getdirentries, *at)
  absent_darwin_ppc.go     new, port-local ABSENT compatibility identifiers
  asm_darwin_ppc.s         new, port-local Syscall*/RawSyscall* → std forwarding
  zsyscall_darwin_ppc.go   new, generated here
  zsyscall_darwin_ppc.s    new, generated here
  zsysnum_darwin_ppc.go    new, generated here
  zerrors_darwin_ppc.go    new, generated here
  ztypes_darwin_ppc.go     new, generated here

plus the five files already differing before this work (port commit
ba4a0942cc, linux/ppc): `syscall_linux_gc.go`, `syscall_linux_ppc.go`,
`syscall_unix_gc.go`, `zsyscall_linux_ppc.go`,
`zsyscall_linux_ppc_abi_test.go`.  `src/cmd/vendor/modules.txt` is untouched:
adding files to an already-vendored package changes neither the versions nor
the package list.  A future `go mod vendor` (or an x/sys bump) deletes the nine
files and reverts C1; regenerate from this directory.

Known limitations
-----------------
1. Legacy vs `$UNIX2003` libc entry points (see Decisions 4): corner-case errno
   and semantics of `kill`, `fcntl`, `select`, `shmctl`, `mmap` differ from
   amd64.  Open port-wide decision covering std and x/sys together.
2. 12 Leopard-absent functions return ENOSYS; the `*at` family emulates
   AT_FDCWD only and returns ENOTSUP otherwise.  `UtimesNanoAt` with any dirfd
   therefore returns ENOSYS.  No in-tree darwin/ppc consumer exists today.
3. The ABSENT shapes (`RawSockaddrVM`, `SaEndpoints`, `TCPConnectionInfo`,
   `IPMreqn`, `IPv6MTUInfo`) have no Leopard authority; they exist only so
   generic code compiles.  `SizeofTCPConnectionInfo` is the ppc32 Go size
   (0x6c), not macOS's 0x70, so `getsockopt` cannot overrun the Go value.
4. `unix.Syscall9` is absent on darwin/ppc32 (API parity exception, Decision 5).
5. `Timeval32`, `XSocket`, `XSockbuf` and their `Sizeof*` are not defined:
   Leopard never completes those C types and cgo therefore cannot emit them.
6. `go vet`'s asmdecl cannot check ppc32 assembly ("cannot determine
   architecture for assembly file"), so the frame sizes in `asm_darwin_ppc.s`
   rest on review, the std precedent and the hardware probe executing
   Syscall6 through Getdirentries.
7. darwin/ppc64 tables are out of scope (goppc-proc-mil000.1.6.2); the same
   pipeline would apply, using pmg5.
